1
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,437
We were consumed by bloodlust.

2
00:00:06,520 --> 00:00:11,260
The Shandora warriors, they only
attacked God's Island Upper Yard,

3
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:15,773
because they wanted to regain a homeland
of their ancestors which we took.

4
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:20,477
My lord, you're not thinking
about that again, are you?

5
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,390
Look around.

6
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:24,537
Look at the peaceful existence
of the citizens of Skypiea.

7
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:27,237
It wouldn't be this way
had our ancestors not

8
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:30,500
taken control of the
Upper Yard 400 years ago.

9
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,777
And it is our duty to carry on this battle

10
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,760
to ensure the peaceful
nature of this nation.

11
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:42,482
We've tried to negotiate with them, but if
they cannot abide by these negotiations,

12
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,798
they do not deserve your compassion.

13
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:51,160
400 years

14
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:56,057
I think that it's time for this endless
strife and bloodshed to come to an end.

15
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:58,777
I only wish that we could
all live in harmony.

16
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:01,720
Put these needless battles behind us.

17
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:09,600
Enemy attack!

18
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:10,840
Enemy attack!

19
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:15,173
Is it another attack by the Shandians?

20
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:16,360
It's not them.

21
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:18,057
What do you mean?

22
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,460
It's a man who calls himself God Eneru.

23
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:22,100
What God Eneru?

24
00:01:40,140 --> 00:01:43,337
Did you know there's an awesome
treasure hidden at the end of the sea?

25
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:46,037
And anyone who finds it,
the King of the Pirates!

26
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,591
Is that exciting or what?

27
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:51,347
There are incredible adventures
out there just waiting for us!

28
00:01:53,980 --> 00:01:58,477
Bon voyage, have the courage
that sail and believe.

29
00:01:58,560 --> 00:02:02,377
And we will see a glimpse of

30
00:02:02,460 --> 00:02:06,580
the sun rising on our tomorrow?

31
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:13,757
Back when we first started,
we had separate horizons.

32
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:18,517
Sailed toward different
dreams, things had changed now!

33
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,137
For together we found, we looked
through the spyglass and see.

34
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:28,677
And we know that our hearts
have brought us here.

35
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:32,357
Where the conscious points our destiny!

36
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:36,260
There's no looking back,
take the hell with me.

37
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:42,900
Bon voyage, we can't stop all
our troubles, forget the past.

38
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:47,337
Though the future's
unclear, we still can smile.

39
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:50,057
We know we'll get there!

40
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:51,720
No regrets.

41
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:55,497
Every tear that we've cried only helps.

42
00:02:55,580 --> 00:02:56,940
Our dreams come true.

43
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:02,900
You and those dreams
are precious in my life.

44
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:09,920
A glimpse of the sun
rising on our tomorrow.

45
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:22,477
I want you to stay and take
care of these two, Sue.

46
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:25,442
Because there's something
important I have to do.

47
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:29,240
I have to warn them.

48
00:03:29,540 --> 00:03:33,660
No matter what it takes, I won't
let your death be in vain, father.

49
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:35,930
Sue Sue!

50
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,925
I can't just sit here and cry.

51
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:41,910
Here!

52
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:43,650
Hey!

53
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:47,337
I think this house belongs
to that pretty lady.

54
00:03:47,420 --> 00:03:50,538
The one who plays her harp
on the beach all the time.

55
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:52,240
Yeah, you're right.

56
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,047
This is her house, for sure.

57
00:03:54,380 --> 00:03:57,792
Her name's Conis, and she
lives here with her dad, Page.

58
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:00,254
They both seem like really nice people.

59
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:03,602
They even invited me over
to have lunch one time.

60
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,437
I heard that girl and her
dad are really bad people.

61
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,638
Stay away, or you'll get in trouble.

62
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:11,680
My mom told me that, too.

63
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:14,645
She said they were helping
the Blue Sea people.

64
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:17,717
That can't be.

65
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,937
I swear it's true, they're trouble.

66
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:22,897
My father said he'd ground me if
he caught me anywhere near them!

67
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,580
Your father said that?

68
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:25,670
I see

69
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:29,160
Oh, I'm sorry, I just
remembered your father is.

70
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:32,697
My daddy's a member of the Enforcers!

71
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:34,357
And he's out on patrol.

72
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,077
My mom says he'll be coming home soon!

73
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:38,497
And I can hardly wait!

74
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:40,497
Because I've never even seen his face.

75
00:04:40,580 --> 00:04:43,097
Oh man, I think it is so awesome!

76
00:04:43,180 --> 00:04:46,417
Your dad is one of the
divine warriors and I'm

77
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:49,441
sure your dad will come
home to see you real soon.

78
00:04:57,060 --> 00:05:00,178
Skypeel will be dropped back
into the blue sea world.

79
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,777
I can't let his death be in vain!

80
00:05:05,860 --> 00:05:07,257
I must tell the others!

81
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:09,080
I have to warn them!

82
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:16,020
What just happened?

83
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:19,888
Why did all these ruins
fall out of the sky?

84
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:25,730
Swordsman!

85
00:05:25,813 --> 00:05:27,180
This is not my day!

86
00:05:27,480 --> 00:05:30,421
Don't tell me you fell
down here with all of this!

87
00:05:30,840 --> 00:05:31,760
Yeah, I did!

88
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,900
And it almost killed me!

89
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:35,780
I'm amazed it didn't.

90
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,697
Are you sure you're all right?

91
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:39,486
Yeah, good to see you, Robin.

92
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:40,560
Where am I?

93
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:41,510
What is this place?

94
00:05:41,593 --> 00:05:44,207
It's the city of gold
we've been looking for.

95
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:46,409
Did you find the treasure?

96
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:47,620
I didn't.

97
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:50,308
There's no evidence
that gold was ever here.

98
00:06:16,640 --> 00:06:19,700
Wow, that was one crazy
ride if I do say so myself.

99
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:21,668
I think I want to go again.

100
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,140
Are you stupid?

101
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:26,479
Why in the world did you
hold on to the Waver's jet?

102
00:06:27,660 --> 00:06:28,490
Sorry.

103
00:06:28,573 --> 00:06:30,077
Everyone else managed to escape,

104
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:32,977
and we've been left behind
because of your stupidity.

105
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,236
It's all your fault.

106
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:35,170
Don't worry.

107
00:06:35,253 --> 00:06:36,083
Get us out of here.

108
00:06:36,166 --> 00:06:37,057
I've got an idea.

109
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:40,357
Why don't we make our way down to the back
of the snake and escape out its butthole?

110
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:41,820
Ah! Think again, jerk!

111
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:43,392
That's not gonna happen!

112
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,877
Look, it's the horse!

113
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:49,790
That's a bird!

114
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:57,080
Thanks, Mr. Weirdo.

115
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,442
We just got lucky when we
landed on these clouds.

116
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,060
We left Luthi and Isa behind.

117
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:06,556
I hope they're okay.

118
00:07:06,920 --> 00:07:08,597
Pierre's gone to fetch our friends.

119
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:12,920
And when Push comes to shove, he's
a very reliable bird or horse.

120
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:15,297
Hey, where did we end up?

121
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:16,417
What is this place?

122
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:21,080
Well, to be perfectly honest,
I have no idea where we are,

123
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,593
but it looks like we fell to the clouds.

124
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:25,680
Thank you very much.

125
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:31,295
I've traveled all across the
upper yard in my lifetime,

126
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:33,775
but I've never seen this place before.

127
00:07:45,980 --> 00:07:47,420
Could it be?

128
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:50,440
Is this really our homeland?

129
00:08:07,520 --> 00:08:13,480
Light the fire of Shandora, in the
name of the great warrior Kolkata!

130
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,480
Light the fire of Shandora!

131
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:24,260
We're going back to our homeland!

132
00:08:28,080 --> 00:08:30,800
I finally found what
I've been looking for.

133
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,820
The proud city that my
ancestors protected.

134
00:08:36,660 --> 00:08:37,490
Shandora.

135
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:52,220
I think the snake is
looking for something.

136
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:56,131
Either that or Luffy's doing
something that's bothering it.

137
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:03,680
That snake sure is acting strangely.

138
00:09:09,520 --> 00:09:11,100
I think it's crying.

139
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,637
What's the meaning of
this ridiculous outburst?

140
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:19,637
Just what are you getting
yourself so worked up about?

141
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:23,480
You've always been an annoyance to me.

142
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,760
And no longer.

143
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:29,520
Tell Thor.

144
00:09:33,360 --> 00:09:36,280
My son! Oh, no, Nami! She's dead!

145
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:39,428
There's no way she could
have survived that!

146
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:42,200
Robin? And Zoro?

147
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:44,048
When did you guys get here?

148
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,230
Wait!

149
00:09:45,313 --> 00:09:46,143
What are you doing there?

150
00:09:46,226 --> 00:09:47,837
How'd you get out of the snake's stomach?

151
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,197
Glad to see you're all right, Navigator?

152
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:52,137
Yeah, I think I'm all right.

153
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:55,117
But I'm not so sure about the others.

154
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:58,197
Luffy was still in there.

155
00:09:58,280 --> 00:10:01,037
What was he doing in there?

156
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:03,437
I tried to get him out
but he fell off the waver.

157
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:06,537
Ah, that brat is nothing
but a pain in the ass.

158
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:08,377
Is he aware of how much of a hassle he is?

159
00:10:08,460 --> 00:10:09,497
How am I supposed to know?

160
00:10:09,580 --> 00:10:13,977
Just one hit.

161
00:10:14,060 --> 00:10:16,117
That's all it took.

162
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:20,077
Enaru You destroyed him when my bazooka
couldn't even scratch the snake.

163
00:10:20,160 --> 00:10:23,460
And Aissa, I can only
hope she somehow survived.

164
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,420
Ball cloud.

165
00:10:34,980 --> 00:10:36,080
And a rule.

166
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:42,805
That's no way to treat your host,
now, is it, Shandorin warrior?

167
00:10:43,060 --> 00:10:44,825
I thought that you'd be happy.

168
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,412
After all, it was I who brought you
here and returned you to your homeland.

169
00:10:50,740 --> 00:10:52,260
Don't get so worked up.

170
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,091
It's time for that later.

171
00:10:54,580 --> 00:10:55,880
This is the beginning.

172
00:10:56,180 --> 00:10:58,677
You don't want the fun
to win so soon, do you?

173
00:10:58,760 --> 00:11:00,160
This is a game to you?

174
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:03,520
Yes, and a truly petty game at that.

175
00:11:03,740 --> 00:11:08,152
For all of you, we'll be competing
against each other for my entertainment.

176
00:11:20,760 --> 00:11:21,640
Well done.

177
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:24,477
I'm happy so many of
you've made it this far.

178
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:26,900
I extend my welcome to you survivors.

179
00:11:35,700 --> 00:11:37,940
And now the fun truly begins.

180
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:42,264
This is a survival game to see
how many people out of an original

181
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:47,265
People 81, including myself, are still
standing after three hours on this island.

182
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:50,699
The last person left will,
of course, be the winner.

183
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:53,777
Among you are a few participants
who entered late into the game,

184
00:11:53,860 --> 00:11:56,154
but I've decided to allow them to stay.

185
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:58,652
It will make it all the more interesting.

186
00:11:58,940 --> 00:12:02,881
Now the five of us will continue
on in the final stage of the game.

187
00:12:04,940 --> 00:12:06,720
Did he say five people?

188
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:11,077
Zoro, Robin, Gunfall,
Bazooka Man, and Eneru.

189
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,840
That's exactly five people.

190
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:16,889
Good thing he hasn't
noticed that I'm here.

191
00:12:17,160 --> 00:12:20,101
In just a few minutes, the
three hours will be up.

192
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:26,220
Which means that the six people we
have present here are one too many.

193
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:28,060
He knows I'm here!

194
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:32,380
The one thing I know is that
God's prophecy will never falter,

195
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:34,180
because he is absolute.

196
00:12:35,180 --> 00:12:38,180
I'm curious to see how this
person is going to die.

197
00:12:38,380 --> 00:12:39,657
Will you all fight each other?

198
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:42,269
Will you gang up on
one of the weaker ones?

199
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,560
Of course.

200
00:12:43,860 --> 00:12:46,978
You could all resist your
fates and force me to pick.

201
00:12:51,300 --> 00:12:52,737
What do you want to do, Robin?

202
00:12:52,820 --> 00:12:55,640
I'm not going to kill
anyone. I won't either.

203
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:57,940
I won't compete in your sick game.

204
00:12:58,340 --> 00:13:00,840
And I, too, refuse to take part.

205
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:06,100
Why do you gotta drag me into this?

206
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:14,080
You're the only one dying today!

207
00:13:22,200 --> 00:13:23,620
Insolent fools!

208
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,620
You dare to threaten me?

209
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:32,520
Whoa!

210
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:34,540
This guy's dangerous!

211
00:13:37,380 --> 00:13:39,780
I must admit, I'm quite impressed.

212
00:13:40,160 --> 00:13:42,980
But you have no idea
what you're up against.

213
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:47,207
Even the four of you together
don't stand a chance against me.

214
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:56,740
You cannot comprehend the extent of my
powers and what I'm truly capable of.

215
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:04,380
Look at you, an elderly
buffoon wanting peace.

216
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:07,620
a warrior who single-mindedly
seeks his homeland,

217
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:12,220
and thieves from the Blue Sea who
are only concerned with treasures.

218
00:14:12,760 --> 00:14:14,995
All of you, for one reason or another,

219
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:17,904
seek to save this wretched
place called Skypier.

220
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:21,889
But you cannot, because this
nation is fundamentally flawed.

221
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:25,960
I refuse to stand here and
listen to such nonsense.

222
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:28,751
Now tell me where the divine warriors are!

223
00:14:30,560 --> 00:14:33,240
And what exactly is your goal here today?

224
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:37,840
Why an ascension, my old
friend? What do you mean?

225
00:14:38,740 --> 00:14:43,380
I mean, when I ascend, I will
return to my rightful place.

226
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:46,050
What's that?

227
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:48,828
Are you saying that
you're leaving, Skypiea?

228
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:49,900
That's right.

229
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:53,160
I will soon leave this dreadful wasteland.

230
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:58,541
On the island where I grew up, there were
legends of a place regarded as God's home.

231
00:14:58,800 --> 00:14:59,757
As God's home?

232
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:02,640
People call this place Endless Birth,

233
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:08,540
and there, the ground extends as far
as the eye can see, in all directions!

234
00:15:09,420 --> 00:15:12,740
It's my dream to find
this place, this paradise!

235
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:18,100
Endless Birth, a home fit for a god!

236
00:15:19,300 --> 00:15:23,217
My time spent here battling
over the inconsequential lands

237
00:15:23,300 --> 00:15:27,500
of the Upper Yard has been
nothing but a petty triviality.

238
00:15:31,160 --> 00:15:32,200
Listen to me.

239
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:35,873
I tell you this place that
you cherish is an abomination.

240
00:15:37,940 --> 00:15:38,980
Consider this.

241
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,957
It was born in the sky,
though it's not a cloud.

242
00:15:44,040 --> 00:15:46,628
It lives in the sky,
though it's not a bird.

243
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:53,157
This nation which exists in the
sky is an utterly unnatural one.

244
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:57,020
When we die, we all return
to the earth, to the soil.

245
00:15:57,420 --> 00:15:59,780
But here, there is none.

246
00:16:00,980 --> 00:16:03,300
What exactly are you getting at?

247
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:08,940
You really shouldn't be
surprised by my intentions.

248
00:16:09,420 --> 00:16:14,040
As God, I'm bound to adhere to
the divine province on nature.

249
00:16:16,140 --> 00:16:22,560
That's why this unnatural nation will
be ripped apart and pulled from the sky.

250
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,317
You're planning on wiping
out Skypea completely?

251
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:33,900
It's only natural.

252
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:38,497
Don't be so conceited.

253
00:16:38,580 --> 00:16:42,933
The term god is just the title used
to refer to the leader of this nature.

254
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:45,400
True, but that will soon change.

255
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:50,197
A true god does not
live amongst the humans

256
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,927
like you do and treat
them as his playthings.

257
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:57,040
Former God, Gonefall.

258
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:03,260
You're worried about the
divine warriors, are you not?

259
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:07,800
Six years ago,

260
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,677
your divine warriors lost
a battle against my forces,

261
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:14,160
and I took 650 of your
subordinates under my charge.

262
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:20,377
They served me well until this morning,
when I could find no more use for them.

263
00:17:20,460 --> 00:17:22,080
I told you, did I not?

264
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:28,820
The six of us here now are the only
ones left alive in this forsaken place.

265
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:30,600
Such a shame.

266
00:17:31,060 --> 00:17:32,300
You monster.

267
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:38,280
It's not that I wanted to harm
them, but when I told them my goal,

268
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:40,068
they dared to challenge me.

269
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:44,901
And they paid the price
for that insupportination.

270
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:52,237
They were good men, and they all
had families on Angel Island.

271
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:53,460
Yes, I'm aware.

272
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:56,955
I suppose I'll have to bury
their families beside them.

273
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:01,540
You are...

274
00:18:05,180 --> 00:18:06,700
THE DEVIL!

275
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:08,170
HILL!

276
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:27,520
5 million, 10 million, 20 million.

277
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:36,637
Enaru, what should we
do with this old man?

278
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:37,550
He's pathetic.

279
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:39,740
He's useless. Can we kill him?

280
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:41,667
Just throw him into the sea.

281
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:44,427
I doubt he can even be
used for manual labor.

282
00:18:46,280 --> 00:18:49,417
This shrine, on the other hand,
could be quite useful to us.

283
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:53,500
But what we really need are the
services of the divine warriors.

284
00:18:54,100 --> 00:18:57,688
They could be put to work in
bringing about my ultimate goal!

285
00:18:58,340 --> 00:19:00,960
They will never help you in your cause.

286
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:04,580
Silence you're no longer
in charge old man!

287
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:15,580
20 million volts.

288
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,030
No!

289
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,219
Get away from him!

290
00:19:26,340 --> 00:19:28,800
God does exist in this world.

291
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:30,380
How mortifying.

292
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:33,240
And that God is me.

293
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:40,940
The Devil Fruit.

294
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,040
It's the Rumble Rumble Fruit.

295
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:44,477
If I'm not mistaken,

296
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:48,384
this particular fruit is said to
have the power of invincibility.

297
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:51,880
The power of lightning.

298
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:56,140
But lightning?

299
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,640
There's no way.

300
00:19:58,060 --> 00:20:00,200
A human has no chance against that.

301
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,800
It is time.

302
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:08,220
All that I have foreseen
will finally come to be.

303
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:14,486
The four of you should feel
honored to have survived this long.

304
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:18,860
Now, come along,

305
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:25,880
you will join me as I gain passage to
my dream world, to the Endless Birth!

306
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:29,540
Come with me, come and
fulfill your destinies!

307
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:31,400
Why would we?

308
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:34,860
There I will build an
indisputable nation of gods,

309
00:20:35,140 --> 00:20:37,837
where only the Chosen Ones
are permitted to live,

310
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:40,880
a utopia of boundless and eternal power!

311
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:43,377
What is he saying?

312
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:46,140
I will not let those who are unworthy,

313
00:20:46,460 --> 00:20:51,460
like those incompetent subordinates of
mine, sully the stature of this new nation.

314
00:20:51,860 --> 00:20:56,340
Only those who pass my judgment may
bask in the glory of my company.

315
00:20:57,020 --> 00:20:59,180
And what will you do if we refuse?

316
00:21:00,080 --> 00:21:01,120
No, Robin!

317
00:21:01,640 --> 00:21:02,470
Refuse?

318
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,600
But why?

319
00:21:03,740 --> 00:21:05,340
Why refuse to join me?

320
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:06,697
If you stay here,

321
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:09,977
you'll fall into a bottomless pit along
with the rest of this unnatural nation.

322
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:14,557
I have no doubt you could destroy the
entirety of the Upper Yard in one fell swoop.

323
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:17,160
But if you decide to destroy all this,

324
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:21,328
then won't you also be destroying
something that you cherish?

325
00:21:22,300 --> 00:21:24,000
Do you mean the Golden Bell?

326
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:25,540
Yes, that's right.

327
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:27,173
What's the Golden Bell?

328
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:29,720
The Golden Bell.

329
00:21:32,020 --> 00:21:33,920
Oh, don't worry. No need.

330
00:21:34,420 --> 00:21:36,244
I've already made arrangements.

331
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:40,314
Based on what I know about
your travels across Sky Pier,

332
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:43,049
I believe I know where
the bell is located.

333
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:48,780
I know what you're thinking, and it
won't be long before I have the bell.

334
00:21:49,340 --> 00:21:50,880
You seem surprised.

335
00:21:51,720 --> 00:21:56,260
Did you really think that you, a mere
human, could ever get the better of me?

336
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:59,480
How foolish of you.

337
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:01,930
Robin!

338
00:22:02,013 --> 00:22:06,620
There's nothing I hate more in this
world than a cold, calculating woman.

339
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:14,430
No!

340
00:22:32,040 --> 00:22:33,520
How dare you?

341
00:22:35,340 --> 00:22:36,920
I do as I please.

342
00:22:52,600 --> 00:22:54,020
You've got skills!

343
00:22:54,640 --> 00:22:57,220
And you are completely out of your mind!

344
00:23:07,020 --> 00:23:08,340
Burn bazooka!

345
00:23:13,320 --> 00:23:14,150
Party!

346
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:25,720
No way!

347
00:23:25,980 --> 00:23:28,137
How did he manage to
neutralize the bazooka's blast?

348
00:23:28,220 --> 00:23:29,460
Huh.

349
00:23:29,960 --> 00:23:31,800
You still don't get it, do you?

350
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:34,720
Your energy doesn't even register to me.

351
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:37,857
I'm more powerful than
you could ever comprehend.

352
00:23:37,940 --> 00:23:39,840
The thunderclap reverberated.

353
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:43,377
And that only happens when the
air expands at the speed of sound.

354
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:44,813
That's really powerful.

355
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:48,489
That amount of power is greater
than anything we can handle.

356
00:23:49,080 --> 00:23:49,910
It's true.

357
00:23:49,993 --> 00:23:51,700
He really is made of lightning.

358
00:23:52,440 --> 00:23:53,880
The time is near.

359
00:23:54,220 --> 00:23:55,338
Prepare yourselves.

360
00:23:56,100 --> 00:23:59,437
Soon those who remain will set off
for the endless birth together.

361
00:23:59,520 --> 00:24:02,638
Do you even understand what
a rare privilege this is?

362
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:06,060
And why do you assume
we'll come willingly?

363
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:07,510
Hmm?

364
00:24:10,620 --> 00:24:14,120
I don't give a damn about
your so-called dream world!

365
00:24:16,280 --> 00:24:17,110
Zoro!

366
00:24:17,193 --> 00:24:18,217
Stay away from him!

367
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:19,359
He's too powerful!

368
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:20,880
You need a lesson.

369
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:22,711
Soon your body will know.

370
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:24,760
The power of God.

371
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:44,620
I possess a tremendous power that you
puny humans can never hope to overcome.

372
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:47,160
Can you feel it now?

373
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:49,480
The despair.

374
00:24:55,420 --> 00:25:00,160
If one loses all hope, it is an
experience not unlike losing one's life.

375
00:25:06,480 --> 00:25:09,220
People fear death above all things.

376
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:16,197
That's why people
prostrate themselves before

377
00:25:16,280 --> 00:25:18,751
an insurmountable power and beg for mercy.

378
00:25:18,920 --> 00:25:21,332
It is simply the natural order of things.

379
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,977
Beings are meant to bow
before that which they fear.

380
00:25:24,060 --> 00:25:25,080
It's a shame.

381
00:25:25,300 --> 00:25:27,240
You're bound by your instincts.

382
00:25:27,620 --> 00:25:30,480
I can't believe how
incredibly strong he is!

383
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:39,900
What do you think you're trying to do?

384
00:25:41,860 --> 00:25:43,900
And now, time to die.

385
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:49,300
Are you familiar with the
Sea Prism Stone, Aniru?

386
00:25:50,960 --> 00:25:52,397
Sea Prism Stone?

387
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:55,760
That's a stone that can
counteract Devil Fruit powers!

388
00:26:01,560 --> 00:26:04,880
Well then, do your worst, Shandora.

389
00:26:06,060 --> 00:26:07,080
Sea Prism Stone?

390
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:11,456
It's said to harness the power of
the entire ocean into a single blast!

391
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:14,280
It's the sea, condensed into solid form!

392
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:18,317
If anything can overcome the power
of the Devil Fruit, it's the stone!

393
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:19,230
Die!

394
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:22,117
Are you sure you know what you're doing?

395
00:26:22,200 --> 00:26:24,217
You're aware of the
consequences, are you not?

396
00:26:24,300 --> 00:26:26,820
Your body will pay a heavy price as well.

397
00:26:27,560 --> 00:26:30,957
Why sacrifice yourself for a
homeland you will never regain?

398
00:26:31,040 --> 00:26:34,140
If I must, I'll die. Gladly.

399
00:26:35,680 --> 00:26:38,240
If it means I can take you with me!

400
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,360
Don't do it!

401
00:26:43,740 --> 00:26:44,570
Reject!

402
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:53,640
Hold our true ambitions in your
heart and speak not of them.

403
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:56,000
We are the weavers of history.

404
00:26:56,860 --> 00:27:02,260
Those are the words that were
written on a poneglyph 800 years ago.

405
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:04,840
Poneglyph? Yes.

406
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:09,384
And when those who sought to steal
the stone revealed themselves,

407
00:27:09,720 --> 00:27:14,540
the Shandora warriors of the City of
Gold fought bravely to protect it.

408
00:27:15,880 --> 00:27:17,120
Did they succeed?

409
00:27:19,100 --> 00:27:20,817
Yes, they did.

410
00:27:20,900 --> 00:27:23,337
However, the battle took its toll.

411
00:27:23,420 --> 00:27:26,200
A great many warriors died that day.

412
00:27:26,600 --> 00:27:30,380
Those few who survived vowed to
become guardians of the stone.

413
00:27:30,740 --> 00:27:33,017
They kept watch over
the city and the sacred

414
00:27:33,100 --> 00:27:35,760
monoglyph they swore
to defend to the death.

415
00:27:36,800 --> 00:27:39,800
And you say that's the true
story of our ancestors?

416
00:27:41,100 --> 00:27:45,720
But then the island and city of gold
were taken away to Skypiea 400 years ago.

417
00:27:46,340 --> 00:27:48,928
Since then, it's been
under Skypean control.

418
00:27:49,420 --> 00:27:52,457
Our ancestors fought to their
last breath to defend that island.

419
00:27:52,540 --> 00:27:54,128
And then it was taken away!

420
00:27:56,500 --> 00:27:58,020
The Upper Yard.

421
00:27:58,460 --> 00:27:59,840
That is our homeland.

422
00:28:00,260 --> 00:28:01,457
But at the same time,

423
00:28:01,540 --> 00:28:05,780
it alone holds a history that has
disappeared into the darkness of time.

424
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:09,377
Even though it's under the
control of the Skypeans now,

425
00:28:09,460 --> 00:28:14,100
we must never allow the fire of the
proud city of Shandora to die out.

426
00:28:19,600 --> 00:28:21,120
No way!

427
00:28:22,300 --> 00:28:24,320
He really did it!

428
00:28:35,400 --> 00:28:36,540
Robin!

429
00:28:37,380 --> 00:28:38,210
Robin!

430
00:28:38,293 --> 00:28:39,123
Gunfall!

431
00:28:50,360 --> 00:28:51,760
It can't be!

432
00:28:52,340 --> 00:28:54,440
He's restarting his own heart!

433
00:29:13,800 --> 00:29:16,020
It's not that people fear God.

434
00:29:19,040 --> 00:29:21,600
Rather, it is God who is fear itself.

435
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:28,780
What the hell is what this guy?

436
00:29:31,260 --> 00:29:34,000
Wiper, I warned you, did I not?

437
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:37,760
I warned you of the consequences.

438
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:43,840
And now look where you are.

439
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,520
How pitiful.

440
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,620
You call yourself a warrior.

441
00:29:54,440 --> 00:29:55,780
Don't address me.

442
00:29:57,240 --> 00:29:59,600
As if you know anything about me.

443
00:30:01,040 --> 00:30:02,780
Eight hundred years ago,

444
00:30:04,140 --> 00:30:07,611
proud Shandora warriors fought
for the fate of this city.

445
00:30:08,100 --> 00:30:10,540
They fought to their death to protect it.

446
00:30:11,280 --> 00:30:13,820
I am a descendant of those warriors.

447
00:30:15,060 --> 00:30:17,720
One day our homeland
was taken away from us.

448
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:22,697
For four hundred years, we've carried
the great warrior Kalkurus injured pride.

449
00:30:22,780 --> 00:30:27,133
We've sought to return our homeland
to its rightful place for generations.

450
00:30:27,460 --> 00:30:31,720
And now that I've finally made it...

451
00:30:36,780 --> 00:30:38,297
You're standing...

452
00:30:38,380 --> 00:30:39,437
in...

453
00:30:39,520 --> 00:30:41,660
my... way.

454
00:30:47,540 --> 00:30:50,220
I must admit you landed a good blow.

455
00:30:52,060 --> 00:30:55,657
But what a cheap trick
using that sea prism stone

456
00:30:55,740 --> 00:30:59,497
and on top of that using
a reject dial should

457
00:30:59,580 --> 00:31:02,557
Easily kill the ordinary
user but you shot it

458
00:31:02,640 --> 00:31:07,420
twice and you're still
breathing quite impressive

459
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:15,200
However you're still no match for me

460
00:31:21,560 --> 00:31:23,797
Is that...

461
00:31:23,880 --> 00:31:24,720
a bird?

462
00:31:29,220 --> 00:31:30,800
30 million voltino!

463
00:31:48,560 --> 00:31:51,000
So this has a sea prism stone in it, huh?

464
00:31:52,600 --> 00:31:55,920
And now it's your turn,
swordsmen of the blue sea.

465
00:31:56,520 --> 00:31:59,420
The only choice now is
to kill or be killed.

466
00:32:01,800 --> 00:32:02,630
Keaton!

467
00:32:11,800 --> 00:32:12,630
Zoro!

468
00:32:26,800 --> 00:32:28,137
I don't believe it.

469
00:32:28,220 --> 00:32:30,300
Even Zoro.

470
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:34,680
Everyone has fallen to him.

471
00:32:43,900 --> 00:32:45,940
How could he?

472
00:32:54,880 --> 00:32:56,280
Unreal.

473
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:04,460
Even as hurt as he is, he
still intends to fight.

474
00:33:07,880 --> 00:33:09,197
What do you hope to prove?

475
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:10,868
You're going to die anyway.

476
00:33:11,060 --> 00:33:13,001
Why not make it easy on yourself?

477
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:17,780
Did you say it's been 400 years?

478
00:33:18,260 --> 00:33:19,540
For all that time,

479
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:22,977
you and the Shendorians have been
fighting to take back your homeland.

480
00:33:23,060 --> 00:33:26,617
And yet, you are the only warrior
who has managed to make it here.

481
00:33:26,700 --> 00:33:31,417
No wonder this nation will soon fall to
the Blue Sea and be lost for all eternity.

482
00:33:31,500 --> 00:33:33,060
How could he do that?

483
00:33:35,040 --> 00:33:37,160
You're fighting for a lost cause.

484
00:33:37,580 --> 00:33:40,537
Can't you see that you'll
never regain your homeland?

485
00:33:40,620 --> 00:33:41,620
He's unstoppable.

486
00:33:41,940 --> 00:33:43,740
So why get back up?

487
00:33:47,640 --> 00:33:49,160
For my ancestors.

488
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:58,857
I must confess I was
hoping for a better answer

489
00:33:58,940 --> 00:34:01,597
than that but then again
I doubt you're even!

490
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:02,915
Completely conscious?

491
00:34:08,700 --> 00:34:09,530
Wiper.

492
00:34:10,660 --> 00:34:11,840
Look out!

493
00:34:12,580 --> 00:34:13,960
Wiper, come here.

494
00:34:17,040 --> 00:34:17,960
What is it?

495
00:34:21,980 --> 00:34:25,392
Since you are a descendant of
the great warrior Kal 'gara,

496
00:34:25,560 --> 00:34:27,697
I feel I must impart this to you.

497
00:34:27,780 --> 00:34:31,817
Not many know the real reason
Kal 'gara wanted to regain the

498
00:34:31,900 --> 00:34:35,920
homeland and why he would stop
at nothing to do so So tell me,

499
00:34:36,400 --> 00:34:37,753
what's the real reason?

500
00:34:38,240 --> 00:34:39,070
You see,

501
00:34:39,280 --> 00:34:42,137
Kal 'gara felt that the
loss of his homeland

502
00:34:42,220 --> 00:34:45,860
was his greatest failure The problem was,

503
00:34:46,080 --> 00:34:50,580
he lost something else
important to him El Thor

504
00:35:16,540 --> 00:35:20,440
Of all who stood before me,
you are the only one left.

505
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:44,270
I...

506
00:35:44,353 --> 00:35:45,183
Just hear me out.

507
00:35:51,680 --> 00:35:52,777
I want to...

508
00:35:52,860 --> 00:35:54,240
I want to go with you.

509
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:01,637
I've always wanted to go to endless birth

510
00:36:01,720 --> 00:36:04,097
to your dream world

511
00:36:04,180 --> 00:36:09,960
can I come with you
